  <div class="article-wrap">
    <h2 class="article-h3">What guides us through adversity and challenges</h2>
    <blockquote class="article-quote">"Thou implantedst thy highest aim into the heart of those passions: then became they thy virtues and joys." — Nietzsche, <em>Thus Spoke Zarathustra</em>, translated by Thomas Common</blockquote>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p>We believe that the professional business of dealing with companies and people can sometimes lead to <em>uncertainty and ambiguity</em>, so we wrote a list of <b>practical principles</b> to make <b>the way we work</b> transparent:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Treat everyone with respect, whatever their position or nature.</li>
        <li>Always stay open to new knowledge, opportunities and solutions.</li>
        <li>Keep dialogue and communication clear in every project and role.</li>
        <li>Observe, plan and carry out tasks with clear results in mind.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>With this in mind, we work to keep improving lives and businesses, focused on delivering results and solutions without losing a friendly, easy-going relationship with our clients and partners. We deal with logic, rationality and exact thinking all the time; that is why we value personal, well-meaning contact in every relationship we have.</p>
    </div>

